cepted boolean, call_id, normalized_gain. Return sorted by call order (stable order) as list of diagnostics, and accepted_call_ids list of accepted call_ids in order.\n\nThreshold is 0.05 in fixtures. Return result object with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nEdge cases: parseable false -> not accepted regardless of gain. Also if prediction_tokens is zero? Not in fixtures, but to be safe, if prediction_tokens <=0 maybe treat as zero gain? But instruction says \"at least one prediction token\" implying tokens >0. If zero, normalized_gain would be infinite? But we can handle by dividing by max(prediction_tokens, 1) or raise error. I'll assume prediction_tokens >=1, but to be safe, we can check and if prediction_tokens <=0, set normalized_gain to 0? Or raise ValueError. Better to follow \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\". So if prediction_tokens <=0, raise ValueError.\n\nWe need to output diagnostics in supplied call order. So just iterate over calls list as given.\n\nAlso note: \"normalized_weights\" - not mentioned; \"stronger_counterfactual\" - not needed? The objective says \"Use only quantities present in the case payload\". So we use only loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable, threshold. The other mentioned properties are likely from the spec but not present as fields; we just follow what's in payload.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case) that returns dict with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nReturn value must be JSON serializable (list/s of strings, list of objects with boolean, string, number).\n\nTest with fixtures: we can compute expected.\n\nLet's write the code.\n\nWe'll need to import nothing else.\n\nImplementation function.\n\nAlso note: \"accepted_call_ids\" should be list of strings, in order of accepted calls as they appear.\n\nI'll produce the Python source as a string inside JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2137,"completion_tokens":835,"to